// `use` takes a module path (constructs/use.c, research/001 §12.1:
// `ImportPath ::= ("@" "/")? Identifier (("." | "/") Identifier)*` — the
// `@/` root and `/` separator forms are exercised by root_import.astra).
// The seed parses the declaration and discards it: the driver compiles
// exactly one file, so module resolution is deliberately not its job
// (research/002 §5.2).
//
// This case exists because nothing covered `use` at all. With no test to hold
// it in place the parser had drifted from its own grammar and matched `::`
// instead of `.`; Phase 2.2 adopted the dot form (see
// PHASE2_GAP_ANALYSIS.md App. B #6).
// EXPECT: 1
use std.io
use geometry.mesh
use a.b.c

let x = 1
print(x);
